From 2affd1d6af36fdfc8c8367800676528adc9b7519 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PD rockets contributor <contributor@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 07:35:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 130/132] Show where a dropped card lands until the board's
 host confirms the move

On a slow connection a dropped card stays in its old lane until the server's answer arrives. A board with data-kanban-landing now shows a marker the size of the card where the person dropped it, and opens room for it in the target lane, while the card itself stays where the server put it. The marker lives in <body>, out of reach of the morphs that patch the lanes, and follows its slot until the card arrives there (it then animates from the marker), until the page calls the host's releaseLanding() for a refused move, or until data-kanban-landing-timeout (ten seconds by default) runs out. Each ending emits pd-kanban-landing-end. Keyboard moves get the same marker. The marker is a copy of the card marked data-landing-marker, aria-hidden and inert, and takes its look from --pd-landing-opacity and --pd-landing-outline, which default to a Highlight outline in forced colours.
